WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.004
The moment has come.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.300
This show, it's so beautiful.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:13.096
I call it the See family and over
the last three and a half years

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:14.264
we've become so close.

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:17.392
We felt that we have
accomplished something

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:19.144
really big and exciting together

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.356
This is the last time
I'm doing a role like this,

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:24.483
I'm gonna give it
everything I've got.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.950
Something's different.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:35.869
The children

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.996
they have the ability to see.

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:40.999
Now they will come for us.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.338
I like to have fun
and this show is unbelievable

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:50.259
I love being a father,
I love fighting for my family

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.678
and I love Baba just
sacrificing himself

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:53.845
so that they can win.

00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:57.641
It's been a long time brother.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.523
What made this show special is
it's a show about family,

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:06.900
it's a show about a father,
a mother and two children

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.195
trying to figure out their lives
in a very complicated world.

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.574
The level of imagination
is just out of this world.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.288
Everyone that's been on this
show from props, sets, costumes

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:20.872
just cares about it and loves it

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.708
and works so hard
to make it special

00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:24.126
and theres just nothing like it.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.297
What I love about this show,

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:31.008
that's about people that
don't have sight is

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:34.261
they're heroes, and bad-guys,
and they have emotions

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.513
and they're looked at in a way
that people without sight

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:37.597
have never been looked at.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:43.437
Our goal was to make it the
most respectful show

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:45.731
making sure that we change

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:46.857
the world of entertainment

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:48.442
for people who are blind
or low vision.

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:49.526
Fire!

00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:59.119
Joe Strechay's
absolutely invaluable

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.038
there wouldn't be
a show without him.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.124
He's a producer, he's blind

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:08.128
and he's there to further the
development of the characters

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.504
in the best way possible.

00:02:10.005 --> 00:02:12.132
We're gonna use our ears
to listen, right?

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.134
We're not looking at him speak

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.969
we're listening to
him speak, right?

00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:18.764
There's just so much thought

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:20.682
that goes into how
we build things

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:22.184
because we want
to be inclusive

00:02:22.184 --> 00:02:23.352
and because we want
it to make sense.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.147
One of my favorite
things about See

00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:28.899
that no one knows,

00:02:29.775 --> 00:02:32.152
but anyone whose ever
worked with me knows

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.988
is I'm a natural born thief.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.031
Look at that.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.658
That's gonna look
great in my trailer.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.659
[laughs]

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.580
It was definitely the
most challenging production

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.166
There was a really great
sense of camaraderie on set

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.334
and I think everyone was just

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.127
really excited to see this
through to it's completion.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.173
One of the best
things about playing

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.633
a character on a long-form series

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:57.636
like this is you get to
grow with the character.

00:02:57.636 --> 00:02:59.179
It has truly been incredible.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.807
It's been a very
exciting journey

00:03:01.807 --> 00:03:03.600
going through this life 3 years

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.727
that is a really beautiful
thing about acting,

00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.396
you know you create a person

00:03:07.396 --> 00:03:09.898
and you can step into
their body for a while.

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:11.400
Then you sort of
let them go.

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:13.527
You might hate me...

00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:15.612
but I know you
still love me.

00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:18.615
From day 1,

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.784
we just all kind of melted
together in a way

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:23.036
that felt really
nice and natural

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.205
and I'm gonna miss
that the most I think.

00:03:26.832 --> 00:03:29.376
I remember the first
time I met Jason Momoa,

00:03:29.376 --> 00:03:32.045
he came in with such
a presence and energy.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.172
His creativity just
blew my mind.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.217
It's basically me being
a 6 year old boy.

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:38.510
Dream come true.

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:39.636
This kind of roll

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.721
is someone who I
was in a past life.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.433
Living out every childhood
fantasy I ever had.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.017
Look at that.

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:47.853
It's like, I want swords
and this

00:03:47.853 --> 00:03:49.062
and this can have
knuckle knives.

00:03:50.105 --> 00:03:51.106
I love my job.

00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:53.233
[laughs]

00:03:54.276 --> 00:03:55.360
During season 2,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.736
I tore my bicep

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.821
and I had have laser surgery

00:03:57.821 --> 00:03:58.989
just to kind of
keep my arm on.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:00.073
So when I'm fighting Bautista

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.241
the whole
time it's taped on.

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:02.325
Look at that...

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:05.245
my shoulder is hanging
on by a thread.

00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:07.664
Jason really
dedicated everything.

00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:09.749
His body, his emotions,

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.251
and made that character

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.462
the ultimate hero,
the ultimate father,

00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:15.046
the ultimate warrior.

00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:17.883
[screams]

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.682
I'm gonna miss my people.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.684
These are really our people.

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:29.978
And...

00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:31.897
we created something
really special here.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.983
You're not just my family.

00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:37.903
You're the best that I
have ever known.

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:41.031
We're really good friends

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.699
and we look after each other.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:44.451
The book of Baba.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.621
Wow.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.791
Beautiful.

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:56.171
We grew together and we
reinforced together

00:04:56.171 --> 00:04:57.714
in a way that I
never experienced

00:04:57.714 --> 00:04:58.924
with a film team before.

00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:01.384
As a token of my appreciation.

00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:02.427
Holy smokes.

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:04.054
There's your dream guitar buddy.

00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:05.805
Look at that.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.057
How beautiful.
-Sunshine.

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:08.350
Rays of light like you buddy.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.101
Thank you so much,

00:05:10.101 --> 00:05:11.394
Thank you so much.

00:05:13.605 --> 00:05:16.358
We've gone through a journey
within the show

00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:19.027
and also a journey
within the world.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:20.278
You know, with everything
that's been going on

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.863
in the past 3 years,
I mean we shared it

00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:23.657
all together, like a tribe

00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:25.158
and so I'll miss that.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.537
I will die before I allow
anything to happen to you.

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:33.291
Baba Voss,
he's awesome.

00:05:34.084 --> 00:05:35.919
It's a character that
I can honestly say

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:37.504
is my favorite character
I've ever played

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:39.381
and I know I gave
everything to it and

00:05:39.381 --> 00:05:41.383
I will enjoy watching it
for years to come.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.344
I stand with Baba Voss.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.346
♪♪

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:57.732
Thank you very much...

00:05:57.732 --> 00:05:59.192
That's all I've got in me

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.986
I gave it to this, so...

00:06:02.112 --> 00:06:02.988
I'm beat.

00:06:02.988 --> 00:06:03.905
[laughs]

00:06:03.905 --> 00:06:05.532
[applause]

